     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Why does shiny, when using reactive values fail to preserve the class of the columns of a data frame??</p><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Using the following data frame- written to a txt file:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">my data&lt;-as.data.frame(cbind(c(1:10),c(11:20), c(21:30)), \r\nwrite. table(mydata, &quot;mydata.txt&quot;, sep=&quot;\\t&quot;)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Use the below code to <strong>upload the file to be read as a df with numeric vals</strong> and notice how it fails to preserve the class and prevent further operations on the data- Error given below:</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">uinew &lt;- dashboardPage(\r\n   dashboardHeader(title=&quot;zoom&quot;),\r\n   dashboardSidebar(),\r\n   dashboardBody(\r\n     fileInput(&#39;file1&#39;, &#39;Choose file to upload&#39;,\r\n        accept = c(\r\n          &#39;text/csv&#39;,\r\n          &#39;text/comma-separated-values&#39;,\r\n          &#39;text/tab-separated-values&#39;,\r\n          &#39;text/plain&#39;,\r\n          &#39;.csv&#39;,\r\n          &#39;.tsv&#39;\r\n        )\r\n    ),\r\n    actionButton(&quot;choices&quot;, &quot;Run analysis&quot;),\r\n    plotOutput(&quot;g3plot&quot;)\r\n  ))\r\n\r\n  servernew&lt;-function(input, output){\r\n    g3 &lt;- eventReactive(input$choices, {\r\n      inFile &lt;- input$file1\r\n      if (is.null(inFile))\r\n      return(NULL)\r\n\r\n    t&lt;-read.table(inFile$datapath, header = T, sep = &quot;\\t&quot;)\r\n    t&lt;-for(i in colnames(t)){\r\n      as.numeric(t[,i])\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    p1&lt;-cor(t,use=&quot;p&quot;)\r\n    igraph.to.graphNEL(simplify(graph_from_adjacency_matrix(p1, weighted=T)))\r\n    })\r\n  output$g3plot = renderPlot({\r\n    plot.igraph(g3(), layout=layout.mds)\r\n  })\r\n  }\r\nshinyApp(uinew, servernew)\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">Despite my attempt to convert the columns of the read data frame with the &#39;for loop&#39;.</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:1em;padding:5px;width:auto;max-height:600px;overflow:auto;font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;background-color:rgb(239,240,241);word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(36,39,41)\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,sans-serif;white-space:inherit\">Warning: Error in array: &#39;data&#39; must be of a vector type, was &#39;NULL&#39;\r\nStack trace (innermost first):\r\n   105: array\r\n   104: as.matrix.default\r\n   103: as.matrix\r\n   102: cor\r\n   101: eventReactiveHandler [~/Alireza/debug.R#30]\r\n</code></pre><p style=\"margin-bottom:1em;font-size:15px;clear:both;color:rgb(36,39,41);font-family:Arial,&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,sans-serif\">How can I preserve the class of the data frame through the consecutive rounds of analysis?</p></div>"
